      "updated": 1781413104121,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- Admins can add, update, and remove hotels and room types.\n- Admins can adjust pricing and inventory.\n- Users can search for hotels by location, dates, guest count, price\nrange, and amenities.\n- Users can book rooms, view reservations, and cancel bookings.\n- System must prevent double bookings (Strong Consistency).\n- System must process payments and handle failures gracefully.\n- System must send notifications for confirmations, cancellations, and\npayments.\n\n-- Out of Scope \n- Detailed user reviews and ratings.\n- Offline booking syncing.\n- Real-time customer support chat.\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- 10M Daily Active Users (DAU) / Visits\n- 1M Bookings per day\n- 100,000 Hotels globally\n- 10M Rooms total on the platform\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: Scale horizontally without redesigning the core system.\n- Performance: Search latency under 500ms; Booking confirmation in 2-3\nseconds.\n- Availability: 99.9%+ uptime.\n- Reliability: Relational Database utilized for ACID guarantees\n(atomicity, consistency, isolation, durability).\n- Consistency: Strong consistency is non-negotiable (prevent double\nbooking of the same room/dates).\n- Concurrency: Handle thousands of simultaneous booking attempts for\nthe same hotel.\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS : 10*(10M DAU)/ (10^5) => 1000\n    > Write QPS : 1*(1M Bookings)/ (10^5) => 10\n    > Peak QPS\n        Approximate: Peak QPS ≈ 3000 (Read) / 30 (Write)\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 1M daily writes × 1 KB average request = 1 GB\n    > Yearly storage = 1 GB × 365 = 365 GB\n    > Total storage (5-year plan)\n    > Total storage = 365 GB × 5 = 1.82 TB\n    > Total physical storage ≈ 1.82 TB × 3 = 5.46 TB\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 10 write QPS × 1 KB average write = 10 KB/s\n    > Egress = 1000 read QPS × 100 KB average read = 100 MB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 100M daily read requests × 100 KB× 0.20 = 2 TB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- Hotel: hotel_id (PK), name, address, location\n- Room_Type_Rate: hotel_id (PK), date (PK), rate\n- Guest: guest_id (PK), first_name, last_name, email\n- Room: room_id (PK), room_type_id, floor, number, hotel_id, name,\nis_available\n- Reservation: reservation_id (PK), hotel_id, room_id, start_date,\nend_date, status, guest_id\n\n6) API Design \n\nGET /v1/hotels/{id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {hotel_details}\n\nPOST /v1/hotels\n    Input: {hotel_metadata}\n    Output: 201 Created\n\nPUT /v1/hotels/{id}\n    Input: {updated_hotel_metadata}\n    Output: 200 OK\n\nDELETE /v1/hotels/{id}\n    Output: 204 No Content\n\nGET /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms/{room_id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {room_type_details}\n\nPOST /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms\n    Input: {room_metadata}\n    Output: 201 Created\n\nPUT /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms/{room_id}\n    Input: {updated_room_metadata}\n    Output: 200 OK\n\nDELETE /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms/{room_id}\n    Output: 204 No Content\n\nGET /v1/reservations\n    Output: 200 OK, [{reservation_history}]\n\nGET /v1/reservations/{id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {reservation_details}\n\nPOST /v1/reservations\n    Input: {hotel_id, room_type_id, start_date, end_date, guest_id}\n    Output: 201 Created, {reservation_id}\n\nDELETE /v1/reservations/{id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {status: canceled}\n\nGET /v1/search\n     Input (Query Params): location, checkIn, checkOut, guests, beds,\npriceRange\n    Output: 200 OK, [{available_hotels_and_room_types}]\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- Admins can add, update, and remove hotels and room types.\n- Admins can adjust pricing and inventory.\n- Users can search for hotels by location, dates, guest count, price range, and amenities.\n- Users can book rooms, view reservations, and cancel bookings.\n- System must prevent double bookings (Strong Consistency).\n- System must process payments and handle failures gracefully.\n- System must send notifications for confirmations, cancellations, and payments.\n\n-- Out of Scope \n- Detailed user reviews and ratings.\n- Offline booking syncing.\n- Real-time customer support chat.\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- 10M Daily Active Users (DAU) / Visits\n- 1M Bookings per day\n- 100,000 Hotels globally\n- 10M Rooms total on the platform\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: Scale horizontally without redesigning the core system.\n- Performance: Search latency under 500ms; Booking confirmation in 2-3 seconds.\n- Availability: 99.9%+ uptime.\n- Reliability: Relational Database utilized for ACID guarantees (atomicity, consistency, isolation, durability).\n- Consistency: Strong consistency is non-negotiable (prevent double booking of the same room/dates).\n- Concurrency: Handle thousands of simultaneous booking attempts for the same hotel.\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS : 10*(10M DAU)/ (10^5) => 1000\n    > Write QPS : 1*(1M Bookings)/ (10^5) => 10\n    > Peak QPS\n        Approximate: Peak QPS ≈ 3000 (Read) / 30 (Write)\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 1M daily writes × 1 KB average request = 1 GB\n    > Yearly storage = 1 GB × 365 = 365 GB\n    > Total storage (5-year plan)\n    > Total storage = 365 GB × 5 = 1.82 TB\n    > Total physical storage ≈ 1.82 TB × 3 = 5.46 TB\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 10 write QPS × 1 KB average write = 10 KB/s\n    > Egress = 1000 read QPS × 100 KB average read = 100 MB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 100M daily read requests × 100 KB× 0.20 = 2 TB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- Hotel: hotel_id (PK), name, address, location\n- Room_Type_Rate: hotel_id (PK), date (PK), rate\n- Guest: guest_id (PK), first_name, last_name, email\n- Room: room_id (PK), room_type_id, floor, number, hotel_id, name, is_available\n- Reservation: reservation_id (PK), hotel_id, room_id, start_date, end_date, status, guest_id\n\n6) API Design \n\nGET /v1/hotels/{id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {hotel_details}\n\nPOST /v1/hotels\n    Input: {hotel_metadata}\n    Output: 201 Created\n\nPUT /v1/hotels/{id}\n    Input: {updated_hotel_metadata}\n    Output: 200 OK\n\nDELETE /v1/hotels/{id}\n    Output: 204 No Content\n\nGET /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms/{room_id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {room_type_details}\n\nPOST /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms\n    Input: {room_metadata}\n    Output: 201 Created\n\nPUT /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms/{room_id}\n    Input: {updated_room_metadata}\n    Output: 200 OK\n\nDELETE /v1/hotels/{id}/rooms/{room_id}\n    Output: 204 No Content\n\nGET /v1/reservations\n    Output: 200 OK, [{reservation_history}]\n\nGET /v1/reservations/{id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {reservation_details}\n\nPOST /v1/reservations\n    Input: {hotel_id, room_type_id, start_date, end_date, guest_id}\n    Output: 201 Created, {reservation_id}\n\nDELETE /v1/reservations/{id}\n    Output: 200 OK, {status: canceled}\n\nGET /v1/search\n     Input (Query Params): location, checkIn, checkOut, guests, beds, priceRange\n    Output: 200 OK, [{available_hotels_and_room_types}]\n",
